# Gecko Hostel — public UI (canonical direction)

**Scope:** This rule applies **only** when editing the files matched by `globs` above — public marketing and guest booking shell. **Do not** apply this visual system to `components/admin/**`, `pages/AdminPage.tsx`, `pages/AdminLoginPage.tsx`, or other dashboard code.

## Source of truth

- Read and follow **`docs/ui-direction.md`** (repo root) for typography, spacing, imagery, motion, color restraint, and UX flow (cinematic editorial hospitality; premium surf/travel identity).
- Beach Break–style references are **philosophy only** — never clone layouts or assets.

## Must prioritize

- Cinematic, breathable, premium-calm layouts; **photography-led** sections.
- Large vertical rhythm (`py-24`–`32` class of spacing), generous whitespace, clear hierarchy.
- Elegant modern **sans** for primary UI type; **accent** display/handcrafted type **sparingly** (micro-labels only), per `docs/ui-direction.md`.
- Images: warm, slightly moody, soft overlays; avoid neon stock-tourism and card-heavy “template” grids.

## Must avoid (public UI)

- Generic Tailwind / SaaS dashboard patterns (dense card walls, heavy shadows, chip clutter).
- Aggressive “book now”–only flows before destination and lifestyle context.
- Playful tropical fonts for primary navigation or forms.

## Motion

- Subtle, slow, premium: fades, light rises, gentle image scale; **500ms–1200ms**, `ease-out`; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Identity

- Preserve **Gecko Hostel** palette and story (`gecko.*` tokens, logo usage) — tune toward restrained luxury, not theme-park UI.

When unsure: **remove** UI before adding; re-read `docs/ui-direction.md` pre-flight checklist.
